title: Appwrite 1.9.8 security patch for self-hosted deployments
date: 2026-10-21
cover: /images/changelog/2026-10-08-1.avif
tags: security, infrastructure, console
---

Appwrite 1.9.8 is a security patch for self-hosted instances staying on the 1.9 line.

- Refresh outbound TLS trust so Appwrite rejects the compromised eMudhra certificate chains.
- Update the SVG sanitizer to 1.1.1 to address its reported security advisories.
- Invalidate cached avatar and preview responses after updating the sanitizer.

The patch reuses migration V25 and introduces no schema changes. Back up your instance and follow the [1.9 upgrade instructions](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates#upgrading-1-9).

